<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<suite name="mam_coag" version="1.0">
  <!--
    Standalone validation suite for MAM modal aerosol coagulation.

    Validates the ported modal_aero_coag_run in isolation against the CAM
    aerochem snapshot tapes (chem_aero_snapshot_test_design.md, Milestone 2),
    method B only: bit-true vmr states are read straight from the capture
    fields via the registry, so any difference at the check target is a real
    port bug (no pack/unpack round trip in the loop).

    Data flow (ncdata = ncdata_check = the "after" tape):
      input   : mam_vmr_postnewnuc  <- aerochem_vmr_postnewnuc (P2 capture,
                the post-newnuc state = CAM's coag entry)
      inject  : mam_vmr_inject_postnewnuc overwrites the working mam_vmr with
                that state (mam_vmr itself initializes from aerochem_vmr =
                the P_end capture = newnuc entry, which is one boundary too
                early for coag)
      run     : modal_aero_coag_ccpp mutates the working vmr IN PLACE
                (dgnum/dgnumwet/wetdens/T/p from pbuf_*/state captures)
      output  : mam_vmr_checkpoint_postcoag stages the result in
                mam_vmr_postcoag, which physics_check_data compares against
                aerochem_vmr_postcoag (P3 capture)

    EXPECTED NOISE in the check report: the working mam_vmr is compared
    against aerochem_vmr (P_end) but holds the post-coag state by design;
    only the mam_vmr_postcoag comparison is the b4b verdict.

    Init-time ordering (same register/init chain as suite_mam_gasaerexch):
      mam_constituents / sulfur_chemistry_stub - register the constituents so
                the snapshot fields resolve to indices (H2SO4 must exist for
                the portable gasaerexch init's validation)
      mam_mode_metadata     - mode geometry + index maps; sets loffset=0
      mam_gasaerexch_setup  - runs the portable gasaerexch init, whose public
                protected pcage state (modefrm_pcage, soa_equivso4_factor)
                the coag init phase consumes (CAM's init ordering)
      modal_aero_coag_ccpp (init phase) - pair_option selection +
                coagulation-pair tables, calls the portable
                modal_aero_coag_init

    No unpack/apply here: coag works purely in vmr space and the constituent
    tendency for the cluster is recovered by the difference-based
    mam_vmr_unpack only in the assembled suite.
  -->

  <group name="physics_before_coupler">
    <!-- Register MAM aerosol species + condensable gases as CCPP constituents -->
    <scheme>mam_constituents</scheme>
    <scheme>sulfur_chemistry_stub</scheme>

    <!-- Init-only: mode metadata + species index maps (also provides loffset=0) -->
    <scheme>mam_mode_metadata</scheme>

    <!-- Init-only: portable gasaerexch init stores the pcage aging state that
         the coag init phase reads; must precede modal_aero_coag_ccpp -->
    <scheme>mam_gasaerexch_setup</scheme>

    <!-- Inject the bit-true post-newnuc capture as the working vmr (coag entry) -->
    <scheme>mam_vmr_inject_postnewnuc</scheme>

    <!-- Coagulation: init phase builds the pair tables and calls the portable
         modal_aero_coag_init; run phase mutates the working vmr in place -->
    <scheme>modal_aero_coag_ccpp</scheme><!-- dropsonde:portable=modal_aero_coag_run -->

    <!-- Stage the post-coag state for the ncdata_check comparison against
         aerochem_vmr_postcoag -->
    <scheme>mam_vmr_checkpoint_postcoag</scheme>
  </group>
</suite>
